\begin{frontmatter}

\title{Conformal Multi-Step Throughput Tubes for Certified Tube-{MPC} Adaptive Bitrate Streaming}

\author[a]{Saeed Zarbi}
\author[a]{Leili Farzinvash\corref{c1}}
\ead{l.farzinvash@tabrizu.ac.ir}
\author[a]{Pedram Salehpour}
\cortext[c1]{Corresponding author.}

\address[a]{Department of Computer Engineering, Faculty of Electrical and Computer Engineering, University of Tabriz, Tabriz, Iran}

\begin{abstract}
Adaptive Bitrate (ABR) controllers that plan several chunks ahead need uncertainty on future throughput, not only a point forecast.
We propose \emph{Tube-{MPC}}: finite-horizon model predictive control over a \emph{conformal lower-bound tube} on the next \(H\) chunk throughputs.
A max-score simultaneous conformal construction controls joint coverage across the horizon; a pre-refill safety constraint rejects bitrate plans that would rebuffer on the tube trajectory; frozen split calibration (\texttt{\_fs}) fits scales and a joint quantile on disjoint traces.
Calibration replays chunk-level effective throughput through the same simulator used at test time, aligning offline scores with runtime observations.
A pre-registered rule selects the miscoverage level \(\alpha\) per trace family on validation only.
On a frozen test campaign (\TubeEpisodes\ episodes per arm), the primary tube arm improves QoE and reduces rebuffering versus RobustMPC on synthetic and real \mbox{5G} suites (e.g., Irish: \(\Delta\)QoE \cici{\TubeIrishDQoE}{\TubeIrishDQoELo}{\TubeIrishDQoEHi}, \(\Delta\)rebuffer \cici{\TubeIrishDRebuf}{\TubeIrishDRebufLo}{\TubeIrishDRebufHi}\,s) with empirical joint coverage near nominal levels.
Broadband joint coverage improves after chunk-aligned calibration but can remain slightly below the target; we report this limitation explicitly.
The executed action is capped by a one-step conformal projector, connecting this work to single-step certified shields.
\end{abstract}

\begin{keyword}
Adaptive Bitrate Streaming\sep Model Predictive Control\sep Conformal Prediction\sep Multi-step uncertainty\sep Quality of Experience
